{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Remember unto Abraham.</b> If they transgressed the Ten Commandments, Abraham their father was tested with ten trials and has not yet received his reward — give it to him, and the ten will cancel the ten (Tanchuma)." "<b>Unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Israel.</b> If to burn — remember Abraham, who surrendered himself to be burned for Your sake in the furnace of Kasdim. If to slay — remember Isaac, who stretched out his neck at the binding. If to exile — remember Jacob, who went into exile to Charan. And if they are not delivered by their merit, what are You telling me, ״and I will make of you a great nation״? And if a throne of three legs does not stand before You in the time of Your anger — kal va-chomer for a throne of one leg (Berakhot 32)." "<b>That You swore to them by Yourself.</b> You did not swear to them by something that perishes — not by heaven and not by earth and not by mountains and not by hills — but by Yourself, for You endure and Your oath endures forever. For it is said: ״By Myself have I sworn, says YHWH״ (Genesis 22), and to Isaac it is said: ״And I will establish the oath that I swore unto Abraham your father״ (ibid.), and to Jacob it is said: ״I am El Shaddai; be fruitful and multiply״ (ibid. 35) — He swore to him by El Shaddai."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:11.729298922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}